{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn6le02ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Maya Angelou is considered by many to be an American legend. She is best known for her six autobiographies, most notably <span class=\"italic\">I Know Why the Caged Bird Sings</span>. When writing, Angelou followed a distinctly unique routine. She did all her work in a hotel room. It would be a tiny room with just a bed. She kept a dictionary, a Bible, a deck of cards and a bottle of sherry in the room.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn6le02ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "She started to write around 7 a.m. and worked until 2 in the afternoon. She was a multi-tasker and would edit while writing. After coming home, she would read over what she wrote that day. It was through this routine, that Angelou successfully managed to write not only her acclaimed series of autobiographies but numerous poems, plays, lectures, articles, and television scripts.", "id": 2, "time": "27000", "image": "engenn6le02ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "She worked intensely. You may wonder how intense her work was. Sometimes the intensity of the work brought on strange physical reactions like her eyelids swelling up and becoming completely shut. Still, she was driven and pushed herself to the limits of her ability.", "id": 3, "time": "51000", "image": "engenn6le02ob02re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le02ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can describe people I admire.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about people's routines.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "